      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "The §6Hydraulic Fracking Tower§r is a machine capable of extracting infinite liquid from §6Bedrock Fluid Veins§r. These are found embedded in bedrock, and when you place a Hydraulic Fracking Tower above one of them, it will infinitely extract fluid from the vein without depleting it.\n\nThis is at the cost of it requiring more power, and also §bFracking Solution§r, which must be automated.\n\nEvery time oil is extracted, a grass, stone, or dirt block that is exposed to the sky is selected by a normal distribution and converted into a dead or oily version of itself. These block variations can support mustard willows but will kill any other plants on them and are affected by gravity like sand or gravel. In the §cNether§r, Netherrack will turn into Nether Glyphid blocks. This occurs in a 300~ block radius.\n\nHere are the statistics for the Upgrades:\n[img height\u003d200]betterquesting:textures/fracking.png[/img]",
